    <dcterms:title>The Mayflower Compact</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayflower_Compact</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc520>"The Mayflower Compact" is a governing document written in 1620 by men aboard the Mayflower. Forced off course to Cape Cod instead of Virginia, the passengers faced potential mutiny from those claiming freedom from agreed-upon authority. To maintain order, forty-one men signed this covenant, creating a civil government based on majority rule while pledging loyalty to the English Crown. It became Plymouth Colony's founding document and an early example of self-governance in America. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 67.9 (8th &amp; 9th grade). Neither easy nor difficult to read.</pgterms:marc908>
